0022: SWEET on Apple's iPhoneOS machine config instead of MacOSX.

Boots 27g-27w met macOS-only kernel paths (shared-cache trust-cache/SIP/owner checks, then launchd's boot tasks
stalling in keybagd and tzinit failing). ios-guacamole runs iOS 27.2 on the same SoC with an iOS-configured
kernel (iOS SDK, no CSR). Same SWEET additions as before: nos_arm_asm/nos_arm_pmap, config_pmap_ppl (0003),
mockfs + sweet_hfs (+ quota, which the built-in HFS uses), no CPU counters. Built with SDKROOT=iphoneos (workflow).

--- a/config/MASTER.arm64.sweet
+++ b/config/MASTER.arm64.sweet
@@ -1,8 +1,8 @@
 #
-# sweet (OnePlus 7T, SM8150): MASTER.arm64.MacOSX plus the open-source
-# arm64 assembly and pmap (nos_arm_asm, nos_arm_pmap), mockfs, built-in HFS and bindfs, no
-# ext resolver (0057). Remade on xnu-12377 from its own MacOSX config (the 8796 file had the
-# old scheduler option names, so CONFIG_SCHED_TIMESHARE_CORE was never set).
+# sweet (OnePlus 7T, SM8150), iOS 27: Apple's MASTER.arm64.iPhoneOS (xnu-12377) plus the open-source arm64
+# assembly and pmap (nos_arm_asm, nos_arm_pmap), mockfs, built-in HFS (sweet_hfs), no CPU counters.
+# 0022: was the MacOSX config (0001); iOS 27 user space on a Mac-configured kernel met trust-cache, SIP and
+# owner checks of macOS, and ios-guacamole runs 27.2 on an iOS-configured kernel.
